Detailed Solution:
1. Family: A primary group characterized by pre-existing, face-to-face, intimate, and enduring bonds (A -> III);
2. Membership of a club: A secondary group characterized by formal, impersonal, contractual relationships formed by choice (B -> IV);
3. 'We': Refers to the In-group—groups to which a person belongs and identifies with, evoking feelings of loyalty and camaraderie (C -> II);
4. 'They': Refers to the Out-group—groups to which a person does not belong, often perceived with indifference or hostility (D -> I).
This corresponds to (A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I).
Hence, option (A) is the correct match.

